21196	motivation	ZA6767	International Mobil	The study focuses on three main aspects first on the socio structural characteristics of internationally mobile Germans second on the motivation for individual mobility decisions and third on the consequences of international mobility on individual living conditions such as family life professional career and well being life satisfaction.The questionnaires cover the following topics for emigrants 1. Arrival at the current place of residence2. Motivation for emigration3. Living conditions before emigration4. Return to Germany5. Current living conditions 6. General questions concerning individual characteristics Analogous the questionnaires cover the following topics for returnees 1. Arrival at the current place of residence2. Motivation for return migration3. Living conditions before return migration4. Future stays abroad5. Current living conditions6. General questions concerning individual characteristics Additionally generated variables education ISCED and CASMIN occupation ISCO 88 .	2	2.1726184
